questions.question:
A plane is flying through clouds to drop a water quality monitoring system onto a lake. The lake is surrounded by forest inside a rectangle 700 m wide, as shown (all measurements in metres). Measured vertically:

- at the left edge: 180 m of forest, 80 m of lake, 190 m of forest;
- at the middle (350 m from each edge): 80 m of forest at the top and 70 m of forest at the bottom;
- at the right edge: 200 m of forest, 100 m of lake, 150 m of forest.

Assuming the system lands at a random point in the rectangle, estimate the probability that it lands on the lake. Use the trapezoidal rule in your calculations.
